tas11@po.CWRU.Edu (Theodora A. Shlien) writes:
>Teleport without teleport control can also be useful... it can teleport
>you into a vault, and then teleport you out.

Teleportation without teleport control can be very deadly.  You might starve
because you can't get to your food, you might teleport into the Medusa room,
etc.  Surely a few thousand gold isn't worth risking countless ways to die.
Use a pick-axe or some safer method.

About tinning kits: yes, they can be nice to have for whatever reason, but
they are never vital.  I've won lots of games without one.  Actually, I only
won 1 game with one;  I had an Archeologist and used the stupid thing a few
times, but I would have still won without it.  Again, it's a heavy luxury
item which is pretty useless.

BTW, using a tinning kit to get poison resistance was a good point, thanks.
